Subject: The profile records the shape of the objects each instruction defined

What this does
  - Each profiled instruction remembers the shape of the objects it defined (one reference, until
    the dump) and whether it defined objects of more than one shape.
  - The dump prints a `W <digest> pc=<n> rshape=<id> rmulti=<0|1>` line per such instruction, and
    the `S` lines now carry the pc of the op that first filled the site.

Why we need it
  The generator promises what a field of a contracted layout holds only if every read of that field
  agreed on one layout. A read's site names the field; the shape of what the read produced says what
  the field held.

Functions touched
  `js_aot_prof_reg` (records the shape), `aot_dump_one` (writes `W` lines, drops the
  references), `js_aot_prof_free`.

No.

